---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Thoughtful improvements"
  description="Release status and development highlights for ENG Drawing Viewer."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="section-tag">CHANGELOG</div>
      <h1>
        Better, with
        <br />
        <span>every detail.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>A record of the work going into a clearer engineering workspace.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="page-content prose">
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>First public release · In preparation</strong>
        <br />
        There are no public application releases yet. The release version, date,
        downloads and checksums will appear together after review.
      </div>
      <h2>The workspace so far</h2>
      <p>
        The current development application brings together sharp PDF viewing,
        temporary MARK annotations, a drawing queue, local PowerPoint generation
        and 32 offline PDF tools.
      </p>
      <h3>More ways to work</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Images open alongside PDFs as one-page documents.</li>
        <li>
          A dedicated PDF Tools workspace organizes conversion, editing and
          review tasks.
        </li>
        <li>MARK can save a marked page as a new PDF.</li>
        <li>The drawing queue can also export a combined PDF.</li>
        <li>Scan with iPhone integrates with Continuity Camera on Mac.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Preparing the public release</h3>
      <p>
        Work is underway on distribution, complete source, licensing and
        platform verification. The Windows application is being rebuilt. These
        notes describe development progress, not a published release.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={url('download/')}>
        Check availability ↗
      </a>
      <p>
        <a href={url('rss.xml')}>Subscribe to the update feed ↗</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
